    <title>Daily Digest 2026-09-16: 1Password's AI patching benchmark is misleading; Show HN: Glu – installing Homebrew packages 2x fas; Gemini Live audio</title>
    <updated>2026-09-16T00:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://islandirie.github.io/my-rss-feed/daily/2026-09-16.html"/>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;1Password's AI patching benchmark is misleading&lt;/b&gt; — Benchmarks cut through the hype — useful for choosing which model or tool to actually rely on. &lt;a href="https://blog.trailofbits.com/2026/09/15/1passwords-ai-patching-benchmark-is-misleading/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Glu – installing Homebrew packages 2x faster on macOS&lt;/b&gt; — Rust/WASM continue to gain production adoption — worth knowing what's newly ergonomic. &lt;a href="https://glu.run/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Gemini Live audio&lt;/b&gt; — New or updated LLM releases affect tool choices across your entire stack — from IDE copilots to pipeline automation. &lt;a href="https://simonwillison.net/2026/Sep/15/gemini-live/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Inside OpenAI’s agentic software factory&lt;/b&gt; — Agentic tools are changing how software gets built — worth knowing what's newly available and battle-tested. &lt;a href="https://newsletter.pragmaticengineer.com/p/openai-software-factory"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Ukodus – A Sudoku galaxy where every solve becomes a star (Rust/WASM)&lt;/b&gt; — Rust/WASM continue to gain production adoption — worth knowing what's newly ergonomic. &lt;a href="https://ukodus.now/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Kubernetes v1.37: Memory QoS Graduates to Beta&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/09/14/kubernetes-v1-37-memory-qos-graduates-to-beta/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Kubernetes v1.37: Pod-Level Resource Managers graduated to Beta&lt;/b&gt; — Kubernetes ecosystem changes can surface new operational patterns or affect your existing clusters. &lt;a href="https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/09/15/kubernetes-v1-37-pod-level-resource-managers-beta/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Show HN: Capsule – Single-file web apps that save their data into SQLite&lt;/b&gt; — Rust/WASM continue to gain production adoption — worth knowing what's newly ergonomic. &lt;a href="https://withcapsule.app/"&gt;Read&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
